# The core's text is checked out with LF line ends on every OS. Its prompts,
# templates and fixtures are compiled in (`include_str!`) and compared byte
# for byte; a Windows checkout's CRLF (git's `core.autocrlf`) would put a
# carriage return in every line ctxloom writes from them, and in the bytes the
# tests pin. Binary files are detected and left as they are.
* text=auto eol=lf
